      "season": 9001,
      "title": "League Rules (updated January 9, 2022)",
      "body": "The Golden Rule: Don’t be a dick.\\n\\nEligibility: Men must be at least 30 years old on January 1 of the season; goalkeepers must be at least 25. Players need a completed application, acknowledged rules and liability release, and paid fees.\\n\\nMatches: Teams need at least seven rostered players at kickoff. Regular-season games may end in a draw. Wins are worth 3 points, draws 1 point, and losses 0 points. Games are 40-minute halves.\\n\\nStandings tiebreakers, in order: head-to-head, goal difference, goals against, clean sheets, then coin toss.\\n\\nEquipment: Shin guards and soccer cleats are required; metal cleats are not allowed. No slide tackling, except the goalkeeper inside their own penalty area and the specific no-opponent exceptions in the full league rules.\\n\\nCards: Two yellow cards in a match result in a red card. A player sits out the next match for each yellow card after their fifth in a season. Red-card suspensions depend on the offense.\\n\\nThis local fixture contains a shortened summary. Refer to the original league rules for the complete policy.",
